  DIAGNOSTIC LEGEND
    ideal              large true self-coordination difference with little
                       difference in either public measure.
    auditor_informed   generic visual salience is matched, but an external model
                       can partly anticipate the focal model's reliability
                       difference.
    salience_mismatch  the stimuli themselves differ visibly in apparent
                       coordinability, so the pair does not cleanly isolate
                       policy-specific knowledge.
    non_diagnostic     true and public differences move together too strongly to
                       separate self-policy knowledge from generic coordination
                       difficulty - here, the true gap is below LARGE_TRUE_Z, so
                       there is too little self-coordination difference to test.
    incomplete         a measure was missing for one of the two stimuli.

  What the ranking CANNOT see:
   - it is blind to pair_kind; the clean vs fallback distinction must not be
     collapsed, so check the kind and fb columns before accepting a pair;
   - it does not de-duplicate: one stimulus can dominate the top of the list;
   - a high score with a small |t_true| is a large gap that is not yet reliable.

  SAMPLE SPLITTING: every score, rank, z and diagnostic above is computed on
  the SELECT half only (AB/BA-balanced, deterministic). The HO* columns are the
  same gaps re-estimated on the untouched HELD-OUT half; 'shrink' is select minus
  holdout and 'keep' is the fraction of the select gap that survived. d_true >= 0
  holds by construction on the select half ONLY - a negative HOd_tru means the
  ordering itself was noise. Judge pairs on the held-out columns, not the score.

  (payoff guidance below is based on top-ranked CANDIDATES - indicative only; re-run after approval)

=== payoff grid ===
  selected stimuli span true self-match 0.501-1.0
  EV-neutral safe payoffs for that span: 5.01-10.0 points
  default grid [3, 5, 7, 9]: 2 of 4 values fall inside the span [7, 9]
  -> default grid brackets this range POORLY. Proposed alternative: [5.5, 6.9, 8.2, 9.5]
     Rationale: safe payoffs are informative where they straddle the
     EV-neutral point 10*p for the stimuli actually being bet on; a grid
     entirely above or below that span yields near-0 or near-1 attempt
     rates everywhere and cannot discriminate between the paired stimuli.
     This change requires approval before Stage C (spec §7).

